// Pre-computed base64 of the exact same bytes as rts_gif[] above -
// generated once (Python's base64.b64encode(), not at runtime on the
// ESP32) so write_http_page_head() (main.cpp) can inline the logo
// directly into the page's own HTML as a data: URI, instead of the
// browser needing a separate /logo.gif request for it. That separate
// request was one of several a real browser fires simultaneously on
// page load (document + logo + the page's own first fetch('/api/status'))
// competing for the W5500's already-scarce HTTP client socket slots -
// removing it entirely (not just budgeting around it) frees a whole
// socket for other things (see kMaxEthModbusClients's own comment) and
// can never itself lose that race again. Regenerate alongside rts_gif[]
// above if the source image ever changes:
//   python3 -c "import base64; print(base64.b64encode(open('rts.gif','rb').read()).decode())"
